# Benign and Malignant Thyroid Neoplasia

- **Definition** - neoplasia arising from the thyroid <u>presenting as solitary thyroid nodule</u>, which can be benign or malignant:
  - **Follicular adenoma** - most are benign but some secret excess T4 ('toxic adenoma') accounting for 5% of thyrotoxicosis
  - **Thyroid carcinoma** - malignant thyroid tumours classified by cell types:
    - <u>Well differentiated carcinoma</u> - well differentiated carcinoma of follicular cells with good prognosis, classified into papillary carcinoma (75-85%), follicular carcinoma (10-20%)
    - <u>Medullary carcinoma</u> (5-8%) - carcinoma arising from parafollicular C cells
    - <u>Anaplastic carcinoma</u> (\< 5%) - poorly differentiated carcinoma of follicular cells with poor prognosis

    
    ![](../img/malignant_thyroid_tumours.png)
- **Clinical presentation** - identified through workup of thyroid nodule
